subcooled liquid states because the temperature at these states is less than the saturation tem
perature at the given pressure. These states are also referred to as compressed liquid states
because the pressure at each state is higher than the saturation pressure corresponding to the
temperature at the state. The names liquid, subcooled liquid, and compressed liquid are used
interchangeably.
