on Fig. 3.5. Next, consider the case where the pressure is less than the triple point pressure
and the system is at state a′′ of Fig. 3.5. In this case, if the system is heated at constant
pressure it passes through the two-phase solid–vapor region into the vapor region along the
line a′′–b′′–c′′ shown on Fig. 3.5. That is, sublimation occurs.
